## Access Boundaries

Use public marketing, blog, Help Center, Community, status, developer documentation, and documented public Data API documentation only. Do not access authenticated presenter dashboards, host/admin areas, live voting or participation flows, event rooms, account settings, signup/login flows, checkout or billing flows, private APIs, customer data, event data, hidden endpoints, or non-public integrations.

Agents must read and honor the applicable robots policy before crawling public content. Agents must also honor page-level indexing controls, canonical tags, noindex directives, authentication boundaries, rate limits, and API authorization requirements. The Slido Data API documentation is public, but API calls require proper authorization and must not be attempted without a valid customer-authorized use case.

